# SPA rewrite. This app routes with history.pushState, so /project/garbacircle
# and /experience/notionmind are real URLs to a visitor and to a crawler, but
# there is no file at those paths, so a static host answers 404 and the page
# never gets indexed. This hands every unmatched path to index.html, which
# boots the app on the right route.
#
# 200, not 301: a redirect would change the URL and lose the route.
#
# This is Netlify's format (the existing portfolio is hosted there). On other
# hosts the equivalent is:
#   Vercel   vercel.json in the repo root (bhavye.vercel.app deploys this repo)
#   GH Pages copy dist/index.html to dist/404.html
#   Nginx    try_files $uri $uri/ /index.html;
#
# /sitemap is the sitemap, not the app's 404 page. Rules match top-down, so it
# has to come before the catch-all. (vercel.json and vite.config.ts do the same.)
/sitemap   /sitemap.xml  200
/sitemap/  /sitemap.xml  200

# Every real page has its own built HTML file (scripts/routePages.ts) with its
# own title, canonical and text, so a crawler that does not run JavaScript
# indexes the page and not a copy of home. A slug with no file is a real 404,
# answered by dist/404.html, which boots the app on its not-found page.
/experience/:slug  /experience/:slug.html  200
/object/:slug      /object/:slug.html      200
/project/:slug     /project/:slug.html     200

/*  /index.html  200
